# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# roughness_geom_demo.mac — GEOMETRIC roughness of the pTP film, exaggerated so
# it can be seen in the viewer.
#
# The film is rebuilt as a tessellated solid: flat back face on the acrylic, and
# a random Gaussian height map on the beam-facing face (N x N cells, RMS bump
# height pTPgeomRoughAmp). Here the film is made 1 mm thick with 30 x 30 cells
# of 5 mm and 0.3 mm RMS bumps, and a 400 nm beam (not absorbed by pTP) is sent
# through it: each ray is refracted by the local facet it hits, so the beam is
# visibly deflected. This is a demonstrator of facet-level roughness; the real
# sub-wavelength roughness of a 2 µm film is modelled statistically with
# /detector/pTPsigmaAlpha (see roughness_demo.mac). Undo with roughness_off.mac
# (which also restores the 2 µm flat film).
#
# Qt session: Run menu → "Geometric roughness demo"  (or /control/execute roughness_geom_demo.mac)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/detector/pTPlayerthickness 1.0
/detector/pTPgeomRoughCells 30
/detector/pTPgeomRoughAmp 0.3
/detector/pTPgeomRoughSeed 12345
/run/reinitializeGeometry
/run/initialize
/vis/viewer/rebuild
/gps/particle opticalphoton
/gps/energy 3.0996 eV
/gps/pos/type Plane
/gps/pos/shape Circle
/gps/pos/centre 0. 0. -2. cm
/gps/pos/radius 7 mm
/gps/direction 0 0 1
/run/beamOn 40
